<ArticleLayout slug="one-shoot-six-platforms-china-variant-matrix" ctaLabel="Talk to the production team" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Launch one SKU across Tmall, JD, Douyin, RedNote, WeChat and Weibo and, counted from the published figures, it fills 24 slots for organic posts and marketplace listings, or 27 with Douyin's paid formats. Four take a frame at the ratio it was captured in. The rest are crops, re-exports and re-edits of those frames. The shoot needs four set-ups, not six. Every one of those counts is arithmetic on published specs, and this page shows the working.</p>

  <h2>How to read these numbers</h2>

  <p>Most of these specs are not read from a seller backend or a creator account. Tmall and JD gate their rule text behind a seller login, and the platforms' creator and help surfaces mostly serve no specification text to anyone not logged in, so no open source reaches the official value for most rows.</p>

  <p>What follows is, for most rows, the most commonly published figure for each spec, taken from eight separate collections of 12 to 24 independent sources each, in Chinese and English, on 10 September 2026, with the number of sources that agreed shown per row. Counts from different collections are never added together. Rows marked consensus had broad agreement. Rows marked contested did not, and those carry the full spread rather than a single number.</p>

  <p>Treat this as the best available public reading, not as the rule. Platform specs change without announcement and often without an English notice at all. Before you build a batch to any number on this page, open your own seller backend or creator account and confirm it there. Reviewed 10 September 2026.</p>

  <p>Rows marked primary are different. They come from four platform pages read on 10 September 2026: WeChat's Channels help-center article on posting requirements, WeChat's Mini Program framework reference, Weibo's help-center video upload FAQ dated 1 July 2024, and Douyin's Open Platform upload API documentation. Each is primary only for exactly what that page covers, and the row says which.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Every value in this matrix comes from eight separate collections of published figures, one per platform or ad format, gathered on 10 September 2026. Each keeps its own source count, and counts from different collections are never added together. The composition boxes and the slot count further down are arithmetic on those values, not platform rules.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: the Tmall product image, Tmall white-background, JD against Tmall, Douyin video, Douyin ad format, RedNote cover, WeChat and Weibo collections, each collected 10 September 2026 from pools of 12 to 24 sources. A statement of method, with no figure of its own.</p>

  <h2>Can one shoot serve Tmall, JD, Douyin and RedNote?</h2>

  <p>Yes, if "one shoot" means four set-ups on one day rather than one frame. Three facts from the published figures make that work.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">On the published record, Tmall and JD main images match. The most commonly published Tmall main image is a 1:1 square at 800 by 800 pixels, on 12 of 18 sources for the ratio and 14 of 18 for the size. For JD, 6 of 6 pages give 1:1 and 9 of 10 give an 800 by 800 floor. What changes is order: every page that names a slot puts the white-background image fifth on Tmall and first on JD.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: the Tmall product image collection (18 domains) and the JD against Tmall collection (24 pages; slot row 5 of 5 per platform), both collected 10 September 2026. Modal values with counts kept per collection, not primary readings.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">The most commonly published vertical frames fit inside each other. Douyin's post frame is 9:16 at 1080 by 1920 pixels on 4 of 4 sources that name one. RedNote's cover is 3:4 on 14 of 14 sources that name a default, and 1080 by 1440 on 13. A full-width 3:4 cut from the center of a 1080 by 1920 frame measures exactly 1080 by 1440.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: the Douyin video collection (12 domains) and the RedNote cover collection (20 domains), both collected 10 September 2026. Modal values with counts kept per collection; the fit is geometry, not a platform rule.</p>

  <p>The third fact is the exception.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">The white-background image is the one listing asset a styled frame cannot supply. Fourteen of 15 sources that address it treat it as a deliverable with its own rules, and those rules exclude what a lifestyle frame holds: a model on 7 of 15, shadows on 6, text, logos and watermarks on 9. It wants one centered, front-view product on pure white, which means a separate set-up on the shoot day or a clean cutout in retouch.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: the Tmall white-background collection, 15-domain white-background pool, 14 Chinese-language and 1 English-language, collected 10 September 2026, counted by domain. Modal values; the set-up conclusion is reasoning from those rows, not a platform rule.</p>

