  <blockquote class="evidence">Built from the published figures, one SKU launched across Tmall, JD, Douyin, RedNote, WeChat and Weibo fills 24 distinct slots for organic posts and marketplace listings, or 27 with Douyin's in-feed, TopView and open screen formats. Of the 24, four take a frame at its captured ratio, eight are re-crops, eight re-use or re-export a file already made, and four are re-edits or page builds. Seven re-use an identical file, so 17 distinct files come out of the shoot.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: arithmetic on this page's slot matrix, 10 September 2026, one slot per distinct platform surface, built only from rows counted in the eight spec collections. A scoping count, not a platform requirement and not a survey figure. Image counts inside a slot are ceilings and are not summed.</p>

  <p>Apply a different scope, say every optional slot or every paid format on every platform, and the number changes. That is why no image total appears here: carousel and note ceilings are upper limits, not requirements.</p>

  <p>The JD column holds the surprise. A separate JD detail page is a common line item, and the published figures do not support it.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">A second detail page build for JD is not supported by the published figures. The most common JD desktop detail width is 790 pixels, on 5 of 9 pages, which is also the most common Tmall figure, and pages that publish both platforms usually give the same pair, 790 desktop and 750 mobile. The widely repeated split between the two may be a difference between sources rather than between platforms.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: the JD against Tmall collection, 9 pages carrying a JD detail width and 6 carrying a Tmall width, collected 10 September 2026. Modal values, contested, not primary readings. Confirm in both seller backends before re-using one build.</p>

  <p>Douyin's paid formats sit at the other end. They cannot be cropped out of anything.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Douyin's paid formats are edits of the vertical master rather than crops of it. TopView runs 10 to 60 seconds on 4 of 5 Douyin-specific sources, and 4 of 4 that describe it say the first 3 seconds play full screen with nothing on top. Open screen shows a static image for 3 seconds, an animated image for 4 and a video for 5, on 5 of 5 sources. Each needs its own cut from the same footage.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: the Douyin ad format collection, 17 sources, pages dated 2018 to 2025, collected 10 September 2026. Modal values, not primary readings; "its own cut" is reasoning from those durations.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Those 24 slots need five aspect ratios, 1:1, 3:4, 9:16, 2.35:1 and 5:4, plus page and body widths that are builds rather than frames. Every square slot is a centered cut of the 3:4 still, so the shoot needs four set-ups: a 3:4 still, a 9:16 video, a wide landscape frame and a white background.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: derived from this page's slot matrix, 10 September 2026, ratios as published in the eight spec collections with counts per collection in the matrix. Arithmetic, not a platform rule.</p>

  <h2>What has to be captured on the shoot day?</h2>

  <p>Four set-ups, each composed so its crops survive. The checklist carries the constraints from the collections above.</p>

